    },
    sections: [
      {
        type: 'about',
        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Slabberjan',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Slabberjan is a traditional Dutch elimination game, specific to Zeeland, where players swap 'pieces' (originally cards, now custom tiles/tokens called 'Doppen') to avoid holding the lowest rank at the end of a round. It is remarkably similar to the card game 'Gnav' or 'Cuckoo'. The game involves bluffing, special 'Matador' pieces that block swaps (Knight, Bird, Cat, Inn), and a pot that the loser must pay into. The last player with chips wins.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Derived from the 18th-century card games 'Gnav' (Danish) and 'Vogelspiel' (German). When cards were banned/taxed, players switched to wooden pieces.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'From two up to twenty or more in the parent game Gnav; the Zeeland variant Slabberjan is typically played with five to fifteen players for the best experience. Since each player receives one piece from the set of 42, two to forty-two players are possible.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '42 pieces. Ranking: Knight (Kap-af) > Bird > Cat > Inn > 12 > 11... > 0 > White Bread > Pot > Face > Fool (Jan Rit).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '42 pieces. Ranking: Knight (Kap-af) > Bird > Cat > Inn > 12 > 11... > 0 > White Bread > Pot > Face > Fool (Jan Rit).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Each player draws 1 piece from a bag. Kept secret.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Variations',
            subtitle: 'Known ways this game changes',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'list',
                style: 'unordered',
                items: [
                  {
                    text: 'Gnav (Norwegian/Danish): Original Norwegian and Danish game with slightly different piece names and order: Cuckoo (stops trading), Knight (cut off), Cat (undo swaps), Horse, House (pass to next). Played with 42 cards or pawns; 2 to 20 or more players.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Slabberjan (Zeeland): Zeeland variant with Ruiter/Kap-af (knight), Vogel (bird), Poesje (cat), Herberg (inn); no horse; White Bread below zero. Played with 42 pieces only.',
                  },
                ],
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
